"1426","Narrated by Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out one day on his mount with his companions walking ahead of him. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Do you permit me to advance to you with a willing heart?"" He said: ""Yes."" So Mu'adh drew near to him and they walked together. Mu'adh said: ""May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! I ask Allah to make our day before your day. Did you see if something happens and we do not see anything — if Allah wills — what deeds should we perform after you?""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) remained silent, then said: ""Jihad in the path of Allah."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What an excellent thing is jihad, and the One who has more power over people than that."" [Mu'adh asked:] ""Fasting and charity?"" He said: ""What an excellent thing is fasting and charity."" Mu'adh mentioned every good deed that a son of Adam can do. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""And guiding people to good is better than that."" He said: ""What is it, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, that guiding people to good is better than that?"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) pointed to his mouth and said: ""Silence except for good."" He said: ""And are we held accountable for what our tongues utter?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) struck Mu'adh's thigh and said: ""O Mu'adh, may your mother lose you! And do people get thrown on their faces in Hell except for what their tongues have uttered?! Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent from evil. Speak good and you will gain, and remain silent from evil and you will be safe."""
